WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:19.929
Bobby grinned when he arrived at camp on Friday.

2
00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:25.630
All the campers, including Mr. Dunn, were wearing their tie-dyed T-shirts.

3
00:00:25.631 --> 00:00:29.441
"We look like a team!" Bobby said.

4
00:00:29.442 --> 00:00:35.344
"Why did you ask us to wear the T-shirts today?" Bobby asked Mr. Dunn.

5
00:00:35.345 --> 00:00:40.926
"Because today we are going to be a team," Mr. Dunn said.

6
00:00:40.927 --> 00:00:43.677
"A business team."

7
00:00:43.678 --> 00:00:48.763
"Remember the lemonade we made a few weeks ago?" Mr. Dunn asked.

8
00:00:48.764 --> 00:00:56.091
"Of course! It was sooo good," Izzie said.

9
00:00:56.092 --> 00:01:00.672
"Bobby said it was good enough to sell," Mr. Dunn said.

10
00:01:00.673 --> 00:01:05.153
"Today we'll try selling it," Mr. Dunn said.

11
00:01:05.154 --> 00:01:09.364
"We're having a lemonade stand?" Nina cried.

12
00:01:09.365 --> 00:01:14.731
"Yep. So we'll need half our team to make the lemonade.

13
00:01:14.732 --> 00:01:21.309
The other half can paint signs and set up the table," said Mr. Dunn.

14
00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:25.583
Izzie, Nina, and Ethan agreed to make the signs.

15
00:01:25.584 --> 00:01:29.434
Bobby and Jason said they would make the lemonade.

16
00:01:29.435 --> 00:01:35.963
"Everyone is going to love this lemonade," Bobby said to Jason.

17
00:01:35.964 --> 00:01:39.550
"We're going to be rich!"

18
00:01:39.551 --> 00:01:42.232
Jason rolled his eyes.

19
00:01:42.233 --> 00:01:46.640
"Um, I don't think we're going to be rich, Bobby.

20
00:01:46.641 --> 00:01:48.782
How much is one cup?

21
00:01:48.783 --> 00:01:51.873
Probably just a few cents."

22
00:01:51.874 --> 00:01:54.780
"No way!" Bobby said.

23
00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:59.150
"It should be at least two dollars."

24
00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:05.983
The boys spent two hours making pitchers of lemonade.

25
00:02:05.984 --> 00:02:09.850
Then they brought a cooler of ice outside.

26
00:02:09.851 --> 00:02:12.956
The girls and Ethan had made huge signs that said:

27
00:02:12.957 --> 00:02:17.477
"Sweet Iced Lemonade, Just 25¢."

28
00:02:17.478 --> 00:02:24.505
There were two tables, chairs, a money box, and paper cups.

29
00:02:24.506 --> 00:02:27.208
"Just twenty-five cents?

30
00:02:27.209 --> 00:02:30.803
Is that a joke?" Bobby cried.

31
00:02:30.804 --> 00:02:33.372
"No," Izzie said.

32
00:02:33.373 --> 00:02:36.481
"It's a fair price to attract customers."

33
00:02:36.482 --> 00:02:40.553
And the kids didn't have to wait long for their first customer.

34
00:02:40.554 --> 00:02:44.274
Soon a woman came running toward them!

35
00:02:44.275 --> 00:02:48.586
It was Ms. Folani! "Hi, everybody.

36
00:02:48.587 --> 00:02:51.385
I was jogging when I saw your sign.

37
00:02:51.386 --> 00:02:55.765
Lemonade sounds great right now," the principal said.

38
00:02:55.766 --> 00:02:58.470
Nina poured her a cup.

39
00:02:58.471 --> 00:03:03.667
Bobby added the ice cubes.

40
00:03:03.668 --> 00:03:08.836
Ethan put her dollar in the money box and gave her change.

41
00:03:08.837 --> 00:03:12.048
Ms. Folani gulped down her cup.

42
00:03:12.049 --> 00:03:15.312
"This is delicious. Thanks!

43
00:03:15.313 --> 00:03:17.744
See you in September!"

44
00:03:17.745 --> 00:03:21.745
She jogged back down the road.

45
00:03:21.746 --> 00:03:28.120
By the end of the day, there was only one cup of lemonade left.

46
00:03:28.121 --> 00:03:33.524
And the lemonade stand had made $10.00!

47
00:03:33.525 --> 00:03:37.600
"We should have charged more," Bobby grumbled.

48
00:03:37.601 --> 00:03:40.584
"We'll each only get two dollars!"

49
00:03:40.585 --> 00:03:46.044
Suddenly a familiar voice said, "It looks like the lemonade stand was a hit!"

50
00:03:46.045 --> 00:03:49.848
It was Allison from Penny's Dog Shelter.

51
00:03:49.849 --> 00:03:55.100
Allison smiled. "I stopped by to say thank you."

52
00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:58.393
"Thank you for what?" Bobby asked.

53
00:03:58.394 --> 00:04:05.016
Mr. Dunn coughed. "Actually I haven't told them about the donation yet.

54
00:04:05.017 --> 00:04:08.856
I wanted to make sure we made enough money."

55
00:04:08.857 --> 00:04:13.622
"Donation?" Bobby repeated.

56
00:04:13.623 --> 00:04:17.127
"To Penny's?" Jason asked excitedly.

57
00:04:17.128 --> 00:04:20.630
"That's such a great idea, Mr. Dunn!"

58
00:04:20.631 --> 00:04:22.825
Mr. Dunn nodded.

59
00:04:22.826 --> 00:04:28.127
"We can donate the money as long as it's okay with all of you," he said.

60
00:04:28.128 --> 00:04:31.227
Everyone looked at Bobby.

61
00:04:31.228 --> 00:04:34.415
Bobby smiled at the rest of the team.

62
00:04:34.416 --> 00:04:36.716
"Of course it's okay."

63
00:04:36.717 --> 00:04:39.057
He looked at Mr. Dunn.

64
00:04:39.058 --> 00:04:48.702
"But we still should have raised the price!"
